# Batch 2 / C3 / G5 — source string literals are exact answers, not symbols.
#
# This case pins the typed `string_literal` evidence lane. The correct answer
# is the literal value returned by EmitAnswerDocument.Name(), grounded at the
# source line where the value appears. The final answer should not route the
# tool name through symbol-definition enumeration or drift to neighbouring
# emit_answer_* tools.

ID="m1_tool_name_literal"
NAME="exact tool-name literal — Name return value"
QUESTION="internal/tool/emit_answer_document.go 里 EmitAnswerDocument.Name() 返回的精确工具名字面量是什么？只回答这个源码字符串 literal，并给出位置。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="emit_answer_document internal/tool/emit_answer_document.go"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="emit_answer_document_patch emit_answer_symbol emit_evidence"
